- *distance between lz and gl genes*

- [Expected\: 10.7 + 14.7 = 25.4 m.u.]{color=#0000CC}
- 176 of 740 have crossovers between lz and gl.
- 40+33+59+44
- [176/740 = 23.7 m.u.]{color=orange}
- 6 are double cross-overs that are usually not counted.
- 176 + 6x2 = 188
- 188/740 = 25.4 m.u.
- how does this work...

=== layout: one-panel

# *Interference*

@body

- probability of crossover between [lz]{color=red} and [su]{color=#0000FF} was 0.107 (10.7 map units)
- probability of crossover between [su]{color=#0000FF} and [gl]{color=red} was 0.147 (14.7 map units)
- expected double crossover rate\:
  - 0.107 &#215; 0.147 = 0.0157
  - 0.0157 &#215; 740 offspring = [11.6 double crossovers]{color=blue}
- only [6 double crossovers]{color=orange} were observed.
- less double crossovers than expected is called [*interference*]{color=red underline=true}
  - [*coefficient of coincidence = 6/11.6 = 51.7%*]{color=#FF33FF underline=true}
  - [*interference = 1 &#8211; coc = 100 &#8211; 51.7 = 48.3%*]{color=#FF33FF underline=true}

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Interference Calculation Lz/Su/Gl*

@body

- Probability of Independent Crossovers\: Multiply individual probabilities of crossovers between genes Lz/Su and Su/Gl.
  - [Calculation\: 0.107 (Lz/Su) &#215; 0.147 (Su/Gl) = 0.015729]{color=red}
- Expected Double Crossovers\: Apply the combined probability to a total progeny counts (e.g., 1000 progeny).
  - [Expected Number\: 0.015729 &#215; 740 = 11.648.5]{color=red}
- Coefficient of Coincidence (CoC)\: Ratio of observed to expected double crossovers.
  - [Calculation\: 6 (observed) / 11.64 (expected) = 0.5155 or 51.55%]{color=red}
- Interference\: Measure of the reduction in expected crossovers due to interference.
  - [Calculation\: Interference\: 1 - CoC = 1 &#8211; 0.5155 = 0.485 or 48.5%]{color=red}
- This indicates a 48.5% decrease in expected double crossovers, showing no interference.

